part.text:
Fixed. The bug: for the bare arg `.`, `expand_glob` in crates/nu-command/src/system/run_external.rs:5855 globbed to the absolute cwd path (e.g. `/a/b/.`), and `strip_prefix(cwd)` returned an empty path — because Rust's `Path::components()` normalizes away a trailing `.` — so external commands received an empty-string argument (git's "empty string is not a valid pathspec" error).

The fix (matching upstream nushell #12950): when stripping the PWD yields a path with no components, return `.` instead:

```rust
let path_stripped = if let Ok(remainder) = path.strip_prefix(cwd) {
    if remainder.components().next().is_none() {
        Path::new(".")
    } else {
        remainder
    }
} else {
    &path
};
```

Verified:
- `shell::pipeline::commands::external::pass_dot_as_external_arguments` now passes (was failing)
- All 49 `external` shell tests, 16 `run_external` command tests, nu-glob (5), and glob-related nu-command tests (71) pass
